<title>FRANCE: Ciments Francais 1996 net rises 16 pct.</title>
<headline>Ciments Francais 1996 net rises 16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			     318  vs	     275</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs) B pref shares  17.50  no comparison</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs) A ord shares    1.25  no comparison</p>
<p>    Operating				    1,948  vs	   2,093</p>
<p>    Cons profit before goodwill		715  vs	     596</p>
<p>    Cashflow				     1,771  vs	   1,868</p>
<p>    Turnover				    12,247  vs	  12,572</p>
<p>NOTE - Ciments Francais, a unit of Italcementi, gave its results in a statement.</p>
<p>It said it has speeded up debt reduction thanks to operating cashflow and asset sales and that the debt reduction in addition to lower interest rates had cut financial expenses, which in turn &quot;more than compensated for the reduction in the operating result&quot;.</p>
<p>Finanical liabilities fell by 1.3 billion francs, or 13 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
